  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}$. Let $\\mathrm{R}$ be a relation on $\\mathrm{A}$ defined by $x \\mathrm{R} y$ if and only if $4 x \\leq 5 \\mathrm{y}$. Let $\\mathrm{m}$ be the number of elements in $\\mathrm{R}$ and $\\mathrm{n}$ be the minimum number of elements from $\\mathrm{A} \\times \\mathrm{A}$ that are required to be added to $\\mathrm{R}$ to make it a symmetric relation. Then $\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
